---
description: 
globs: *.tsx,*.css.ts
alwaysApply: false
---
- DO NOT USE TAILWIND.
- This project uses Mantine as a component library, currently at Mantine v8.
- CSS is written using CSS modules with Linaria. CSS is written in separate files with a `css.ts` extension.
- CSS is imported into React components using `import * as classes from (filename).css`. Use `clsx` (imported as `clsx` or `cx`) for class composition.
- Conditional classes MUST use the clsx object pattern. Never use `condition && classes.foo` or ternaries for toggling classes.

```tsx
clsx(
  classes.base,
  {
    [classes.panel]: isPanel,
    [classes.accent]: showAccent,
    [classes.fullHeight]: fullHeight,
  },
  className,
)
```

Do not write:

```tsx
clsx(
  isPanel ? classes.panel : classes.root,
  isPanel && classes.panel,
  showAccent && classes.accent,
  className,
)
```

Unconditional classes stay as positional string arguments. Conditionals go in the object map (`{ [classes.name]: condition }`).
- Mantine CSS variables are exported using Mantine's `themeToVars` which converts the base Mantine theme object into CSS variables.
- Each css.ts file starts with the following imports:
 `import { css } from "@linaria/core"`
 `import { vass } from "@/lib"`
- Styles in css.ts files are built using the `css` function with string template literals.
